    historyContent: {
      origins: "Troggu is a Swiss Tarot game from the German-speaking Valais (Upper Wallis), played especially in the Visp area, St. Niklaus, and Grächen. Card game researcher John McLeod places its probable origin in the 18th century; the game's mix of Fool-as-excuse and Fool-as-highest-trump rules suggests a transitional form between older Tarot and modern Tarock. A related game may have reached Belgium in the 18th century, evidenced by Cartes de Suisses decks. Its closest relatives are Tape (Fribourg) and Dappen (Baden). After Troccas, Troggu is the second most played tarot game in Switzerland.",
